tract  went to a company run by a close friend  of prime minister justin trudeau a  fellow named  tom pitfield and when the conservatives  found out about the pitfield contract  they went on the attack mr pitfield is  not just the prime minister buddy he's  also married  to the former liberal party president it  certainly  pays to be a liberal insider in ottawa  these days  but as global news has learned it also  looks like it pays to be  a conservative insider in his first six  months in office  o'toole awarded nearly 240 000  worth of taxpayer-funded contracts to  his supporters  and conservative insiders you can't be  giving out the  taxpayer money to your own insiders and  cronies so i think aaron is  has got himself locked into the same  kind of  you know old rum bottle politics on the  rito that people really don't like  that's not all o'toole has also allowed  a top aide  his deputy chief of staff steve outhouse  to run an outside business  that works to help some social  conservative candidates get on the  ballot in the next election  that business's revenue comes from party  donations  i were a conservative i'd be asking  questions of my leader  as to why he is taking sides in  nomination conventions  on the side of social conservatives and  the extreme right  the business arrangement is unusual  o'toole's office says  the house of commons was consulted and  none of it violates house rules  the bottom line to all this those  conservative attacks on liberal ethics  well they've now been blunted and that  work that o'toole's top aide is doing  well that has now renewed tensions  within the conservative party  between the social conservative wing and  other conservatives and  all of this on the eve of a likely late  summer election  farah david aiken in ottawa thank you  david  coyote ugly what's behind a series of  attacks in two provinces  a recent string of coyote attacks is  putting people in vancouver on edge  31 have been recorded in the city's  iconic s